---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Nav from '../components/Nav.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Code from '../components/Code.astro';
import { buildFromSource, buildJobsMac } from '../data/snippets';
import changes from '../data/changes.json' with { type: 'json' };
import checklist from '../data/docs-checklist.json' with { type: 'json' };
import { escape, toHtml } from '../lib/inline.mjs';
import { entryLink, entryMap } from '../lib/manual-pages.mjs';
import { fragmentText, optionId } from '../lib/reference.mjs';
import { citeRows } from '../lib/literature.mjs';
import { BRANCH, EMAIL, PSI4_MANUAL, REPO_URL, shortRev, siteRev } from '../lib/site.mjs';
import '../styles/docs.css';
import '../styles/docs-page.css';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
const rev = siteRev();
const last = changes.at(-1);
const build = last.build;
const records = [...changes].reverse();

// "§<id>" -> manual link (entryLink); a numeric "§N" or an unknown id throws
const link = (id) => {
  if (/^\d+$/.test(id) || !entryMap().has(id)) throw new Error(`docs: unresolved "§${id}"`);
  const l = entryLink(id, null, base);
  const label = l.code ? '<code>' + escape(l.text) + '</code>' : escape(l.text);
  return `<a href="${l.href}">${label}</a>`;
};
// inline markup -> HTML with every "§<id>" linked
const refs = (text) => toHtml(text).replace(/§(\d+|[a-z][a-z0-9_-]*[a-z0-9])/g, (m, id) => link(id));
// headers of the checklist blocks as printed: first line of each fragment, each once
const blockHeaders = [...new Set(checklist.fragments.map((id) => fragmentText(id).split('\n')[0].trim()))];
const option = (key) => link(optionId(key));
const toc = [
  ['install', 'Install'],
  ['check', 'Check the build'],
  ['version', 'Version'],
  ['changes', 'Changes'],
  ['cite', 'Cite'],
  ['licence', 'Licence'],
  ['contact', 'Contact'],
  ['manual', 'Manual'],
];
---
<Base title="Documentation — REKS Studio">
<Nav variant="light" />
<main>

<header class="docshero">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="kicker">Documentation</div>
    <h1>The code: build, version, citation</h1>
  </div>
</header>

<div class="wrap">
  <div class="docs-layout">
    <details class="toc">
      <summary>Contents</summary>
      <nav class="toc-list">{toc.map(([id, label]) => <a href={`#${id}`}>{label}</a>)}</nav>
    </details>

    <div>
      <section id="install" class="docsec">
        <h2>Install</h2>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>REKS Studio is a branch of Psi4 and builds with the Psi4 CMake build; the configuration catalogs are installed with it (<Fragment set:html={refs('§catalog')} />).</p>
        </div>
        <Code code={buildFromSource} lang="bash" />
        <div class="prose">
          <p>macOS, last line: <code>{buildJobsMac}</code></p>
          {build && <p>Measured from scratch on {build.machine}, Psi4 <code>{shortRev(build.rev)}</code>: conda environment {build.time.env} min, {build.disk.env} GB; configure and build {build.time.build} min, {build.disk.build} GB (source, build directory and installation).</p>}
          {last.reachable && <p>Update an existing build: <code>git pull</code> in the clone, then the last line again.</p>}
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="check" class="docsec">
        <h2>Check the build</h2>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>In <code>objdir</code>: <code>ctest -L reks</code>; every test passes within its own tolerances.</p>
          <p>Then run <code>psi4 reks22_h2.dat</code> (download from <Fragment set:html={refs('§worked-inputs')} />) and compare S0 with the table there: they agree within the energy convergence threshold of the run, 10<sup>−6</sup> E<sub>h</sub> (Psi4 default; the input sets none); the last printed digits depend on the BLAS library and the number of threads.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="version" class="docsec">
        <h2>Version</h2>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>Psi4 <code>{rev.short}</code>, {rev.date}: the commit of every output in the manual. Option names and defaults may change on this branch.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="changes" class="docsec">
        <h2>Changes</h2>
        <div class="prose">
          {records.map((r) => (
            <div class="change">
              <h3>Psi4 <code>{shortRev(r.rev)}</code>, {r.date}</h3>
              {(r.notes.length + r.added.length + r.removed.length + r.defaults.length > 0) && (
                <ul>
                  {r.notes.map((n) => <li set:html={refs(n)} />)}
                  {r.added.map((n) => <li>Added: <Fragment set:html={option(n)} /></li>)}
                  {r.removed.map((n) => <li>Removed: <code>{n}</code></li>)}
                  {r.defaults.map((d) => <li>Default of <Fragment set:html={option(d.name)} />: <code>{d.old}</code> → <code>{d.new}</code></li>)}
                </ul>
              )}
            </div>
          ))}
          {last.reachable && <p>Between two revisions: <code>git log &lt;your Git: Rev&gt;..{rev.short}</code> in the clone.</p>}
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="cite" class="docsec">
        <h2>Cite</h2>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>Cite the papers of each feature used. All entries: <a href={`${base}reks-studio.bib`} download>reks-studio.bib</a>; full references: <Fragment set:html={refs('§references')} />.</p>
          <div class="reftable-wrap">
            <table>
              <thead><tr><th>Feature</th><th>When</th><th>Cite</th></tr></thead>
              <tbody>
                {citeRows().map(({ fn, refs: list }) => (
                  <tr>
                    <td>{fn.label}</td>
                    <td set:html={fn.when ? refs(fn.when) : ''} />
                    <td set:html={list.map(({ e, note }) => `${link(e.key)}${note ? ` (${toHtml(note)})` : ''}`).join('; ')} />
                  </tr>
                ))}
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
          <h3>Method name and computational details</h3>
          <p>Name the method SSR (SI-SA-REKS, <Fragment set:html={refs('§overview')} />); in a paper give the printed label <code>kSI-lSA-REKS(N,M)</code> (<Fragment set:html={refs('§si-cassette')} />), the functional as printed in the <code>XC evaluation</code> line, and the basis. The label carries only counts: name the SA-pool configurations with their weights and the cassette configurations as printed; defaults may change between revisions (<a href="#changes">Changes</a>).</p>
          <p>Report:</p>
          <ul>
            <li>the printed blocks <Fragment set:html={blockHeaders.map((h) => `<code>${escape(h)}</code>`).join(', ')} />, which hold these names and weights;</li>
            <li>every REKS option set to a value other than its default (column Default of <Fragment set:html={refs('§option-table')} />), and always <Fragment set:html={checklist.options.map(option).join(', ')} />;</li>
            <li>the Psi4 options <Fragment set:html={checklist.psi4.map((p) => `<a href="${PSI4_MANUAL}autodir_options_c/${p.page}.html"><code>${p.name}</code></a>`).join(', ')} />;</li>
            {checklist.other.map((item) => <li set:html={refs(item)} />)}
          </ul>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="licence" class="docsec">
        <h2>Licence</h2>
        <div class="prose">
          <p>LGPL-3.0, as Psi4: <a href={`${REPO_URL}/blob/${BRANCH}/COPYING.LESSER`}>COPYING.LESSER</a>.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="contact" class="docsec">
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <div class="prose">
          <p><a href={`mailto:${EMAIL}`}>{EMAIL}</a>. Attach the input, the output at <Fragment set:html={refs('§reks_report_level')} /> <code>3</code>, and the <code>Git: Rev</code> line of the output header.</p>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section id="manual" class="docsec">
        <h2>Manual</h2>
        <div class="prose">
          <p><a href={`${base}manual/#tasks`}>Tasks</a>: which input and which output for a task. <Fragment set:html={refs('§option-table')} />: every option.</p>
        </div>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
</main>

<Footer />
</Base>
